# Generated by `next dev` / `next build` from 16.3.0 onwards
#
# Next now writes an agent-instructions block into AGENTS.md and points CLAUDE.md
# at it (node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js). Neither file
# existed in this repo before, and both are regenerated on every dev run, so they
# are ignored rather than deleted — deleting them just recreates an uncommitted
# change on the next `npm run dev`.
#
# To stop them being written at all, set `agentRules: false` in next.config.ts.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Data exports — PERSONAL DATA, NEVER COMMITTED
#
# scripts/offline-conversions.ts writes here, and every row pairs a Google click
# id (an advertising identifier tied to one person) with that customer's true
# lifetime value and first-payment date. It is a short list of identified paying
# students, not aggregate reporting, and it belongs on the operator's machine for
# as long as it takes to upload it to Google Ads and nowhere else.
#
# The blanket *.csv rule is what stops an export written anywhere other than
# exports/ from being caught by `git add .`. The negation re-admits the four
# tracked Google Ads campaign files, which are first-party ad copy and keywords
# with no personal data in them — losing those from version control would be worse
# than the risk the rule exists for.
exports/
*.csv
!marketing/google-ads/*.csv

# Outreach contact lists: names and emails of real people, never committed.
marketing/*contacts*.csv
